# Cloudflare Pages _headers
# Order matters: most specific paths first. The .jsx and .js MIME rules below
# are load-bearing. The app loads modules via <script type="text/babel" src="*.jsx">
# and Pages would otherwise serve .jsx with a non-script Content-Type, which
# modern browsers refuse to execute. Do not remove or reorder these two rules
# above the catch-all security block.

/*.jsx
  Content-Type: text/javascript; charset=utf-8

/*.js
  Content-Type: text/javascript; charset=utf-8

# Cache-Control. Cloudflare Pages does not let a later rule override an
# earlier one for a matching path: when two rules both match, their header
# values are concatenated, not replaced. So these rules use path patterns
# that do not overlap with different Cache-Control values - vendor/fonts/
# assets get a hard year-long cache, the HTML shell and the app's own
# hand-authored scripts do not, and no pattern here matches both.
#
# /vendor/*, /assets/fonts/*, /assets/* - the self-hosted React/ReactDOM
# bundle, the IBM Plex webfonts and the icon/manifest assets. Filenames are
# not content-hashed, so this is safe only as long as an upgrade to any of
# these (e.g. bumping the vendored React build) ships under a NEW filename;
# reusing an existing filename with different content would leave it stale
# in browser caches for up to a year under this rule.
/vendor/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/assets/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# index.html and the app's own precompiled scripts change on every deploy
# under the SAME filename (no content hash), so they must never be cached
# immutably: a stale index.html or pages.js would pin returning users to an
# old build. Short cache, always revalidated (conditional GET / 304s) so a
# repeat visit is cheap but never silently stale.
/
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/index.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/data.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/entities.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/icons.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/store.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/shell.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/pages.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/app.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

# Security headers for every HTML response (and all other paths). The MIME
# rules above already set Content-Type for scripts, so adding these headers to
# /* does not disturb script delivery.
#
# CSP notes (fully self-hosted, browser-only React build):
#   JSX is PRECOMPILED to .js by build-jsx.ps1 (esbuild) and React is pinned to
#     production .min.js, both served from this origin under /vendor/, so
#     script-src is locked to 'self' with no external script host: no
#     'unsafe-eval' (no in-browser Babel) and no 'unsafe-inline' (no inline scripts).
#   No CDN dependency remains: React/ReactDOM were previously loaded from
#     unpkg.com and are now vendored under /vendor/; do not reintroduce an
#     external script-src origin.
#   style-src keeps 'unsafe-inline' for the inline <style> block and React inline
#     style attributes; font-src is locked to 'self' because IBM Plex Sans, Mono
#     and Serif are self-hosted under /assets/fonts/ (previously Google Fonts,
#     now vendored) - do not reintroduce fonts.googleapis.com or fonts.gstatic.com.
#   connect-src allows the production Worker origin (RSS proxy fetch) and the
#     local dev proxy at localhost:3001 / 127.0.0.1:3001.
#   frame-src allows the YouTube live embed. img-src allows YouTube thumbnail + data URIs.
/*
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; font-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data: https://i.ytimg.com https://*.ytimg.com; connect-src 'self' https://aph-proxy.jvega019.workers.dev http://localhost:3001 http://127.0.0.1:3001; frame-src https://www.youtube.com https://www.youtube-nocookie.com; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'self'
